>> title: Classic French Omelette
>> servings: 1
>> time: 10 minutes
>> tags: familiar, watchme, stovetop, eggs, technique

Crack @eggs{3} into a #mixing bowl{} with @kosher salt{1%pinch} and beat with a #fork{} until uniform, about ~{1%minute}.

-- watch: Butter is melted and foamy, not browned.
Melt @unsalted butter{1%tbsp} in a #non-stick skillet{} over medium-low heat.

-- watch: Eggs form small soft curds but still look glossy.
Pour in the beaten eggs and stir constantly with a #rubber spatula{} for ~{2%minutes}.

-- watch: Omelette is just set, glossy on top, and rolled without browning.
Tilt the pan, fold the near edge over itself, and roll the omelette onto a #plate{}.

Finish with @chives{1%tsp} if using and serve immediately.
